Subject: [PATCH] arm64: kernel and runtime_loader fixes R Chromium needs

R Chromium's arm64 package requires haiku_rchromium_fixes, which until now
only a separate system package (the "RENKU System" repository) provided -
and that package has no media_server, libmedia or audio add-ons, so
installing R Chromium on a media-enabled image took the whole media stack
away. These are the same fixes, made part of this image's own haiku package:

- vm: unwire the partial range when locking memory fails part-way
  (haiku-rchromium-arm64 haiku_kernel_patches/K0001).
- runtime_loader: TLS descriptor relocations on arm64, and no x86_gcc2 /
  x86 library subdirectory lookup on architectures that cannot have one
  (haiku_kernel_patches/A0001). The TLSDESC resolver preserves the full
  SIMD state required by the ABI, including the upper halves of q8-q15;
  resolver arguments live with the image and are freed when it unloads.
- The arm64 haiku package provides haiku_rchromium_fixes=1.

diff --git a/headers/private/runtime_loader/runtime_loader.h b/headers/private/runtime_loader/runtime_loader.h
index 39785ed1..d6eb3563 100644
--- a/headers/private/runtime_loader/runtime_loader.h
+++ b/headers/private/runtime_loader/runtime_loader.h
@@ -98,6 +98,9 @@ typedef struct image_t {
 	struct image_t		*prev;
 	int32				ref_count;
 	uint32				flags;
+	// Architecture-specific relocation data owned by the image. The
+	// runtime loader releases this allocation when the image is destroyed.
+	void*				arch_relocation_data;
 
 	uint32				api_version;
 	uint32				abi;
diff --git a/src/data/package_infos/generic/haiku b/src/data/package_infos/generic/haiku
index b2e36c35..8e997950 100644
--- a/src/data/package_infos/generic/haiku
